Z||000005||pontiacs4me||04-27-2001||10:41 PM||||I am 21 and have nothing on my record, ever.  I pay 41 dollars a month for my fiero, and another 19 a month for my firebird.  Thats for liablilty only, but I do body work, so no biggie if I get in a wreck.  Thats with american family insurance.||||reg||1
Z||000006||pontiacs4me||04-27-2001||10:45 PM||||one more thing.  My friend Brent has a 1987 grand prix, and with his 2 wrecks, multiple tickets, being 20, and his DUI about 2 years ago, he was paying 371 dollars a month for liability only.  He went with progressive and got it down to 120 some, he bought a Kawasaki Ninja 650 and thats only 15 bucks a month.  When he turns 21 next month, and the DUI leaves his record, he will only be paying like 80 bucks a month.  Try calling Gieco, or progressive.||||reg||1
Z||000007||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||04-27-2001||10:52 PM||||My 1984 Fiero is $450 per year to insure.<P>I'm married, 30, have USAA insurance, and no tickets in five years.<P>When I was 22,  I had a "Wet Reckless," "Speed over 105mph in a 55," and three tickets.  My insurance for a 1989 Dodge Colt GT Turbo was $4200 per year.  <P>Shop around.  The "fly by night" low-buck insurance guys will pay claims and they will charge you a WHOLE LOT LESS. <P>The reduced my insurance from $4200 to $2100 before any points dropped off.<P>Once you have zero points and are 25, then go with Farmers, State Farm, AAA, or USAA (if you are related to a US soldier).  They are only a great deal if you are an experienced driver with no points.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||04-27-2001||10:53 PM||||For many people, it's best to shop insurance around. This should be done every few months.<P>For others,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> We get decent rates that are hard to beat. I'm paying about $700us a year... One of the benies of having a house and car with the same company. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Nashco||04-27-2001||11:28 PM||||I JUST (two days ago) got insurance for my GT.  I have a perfect driving record, and the policy is in my own name with State Farm.  My parents just got it, so I could get it by transferring of their policy...but this new on is MY policy.  I have a perfect driving record, I'm 19, and this is my only car.  I did the 5 mile drive to work too...they would never check.  My insurance costs 85 bucks a month, about 40 bucks cheaper than when I was on my parent's policy with three cars.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>P.S.  For the record, I hate insurance.  I've never been in any situation where it would help (I'm supposed to be the bad driver as a teen male)...but about 80% of my female friends have had to use the insurance at least once (they're supposed to be better drivers).  Actually...now that I think about it...none of my male friends have ever been in an accident!!!!!  Damn insurance...||||reg||1
