Z||000011||Spektyr||04-28-2001||12:49 AM||||Hehe, well I was the above-average male driver in my young and invincible days.  I probably threw the curve.  Sorry guys.<P>1983 Honda Accord.  Totalled.  Age 16  (Mom's car, was not thrilled)<BR>1981 Chevy Citation.  Spun, frame bent, Totalled.  Age 16  My first car, 1 speeding ticket.<BR>One speeding ticket driving a friend's car.<BR>1980 Ford Granada.  Was T-boned, ruled my fault.  Totalled.  Age 17, 2 speeding tickets.<BR>1986 Chevy Celebrity.  Rear-ended a truck.  Minor damage.  Age 18<BR>1990 Nissan PU.  Wrecked twice (both badly).  Fixed twice (comprehensive insurance)  Many speeding & racing tickets.  Age 20-23<P>I'm now 26, not interested in tempting fate with another opporunity.  My last speeding ticket drops off in a few months.<P>And this only counts the accidents I've been in while driving...<P>Trust me, you're <I>never</I> in that big a hurry.  The accident scene paperwork takes FOREVER to fill out.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000012||jaguiler||04-28-2001||12:58 AM||||Try <A HREF="http://www.gieco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gieco.com</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.progressive.com" TARGET=_blank>www.progressive.com</A> <P>They usually have good rates... I use Gieco..... in a HIGH rate area.... I pay about $150 per month for a 92 BMW and the 86 GT.   ....not too bad....but of course I am married with a clean record......<P>why don't you just get married.... your insurance will go down and you will have someone to nag you about spending so much time with your car.... and on this board....haha<BR><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
